  "summary": "Cold review, iteration 2, of the homily 'All Things Are Ready' (homily.tex, sections/homily/10-homily.tex and 90-note.tex). I verified the packet hash and all nine sealed input hashes. Every homily-owned file, both research records it relies on, the leaf format and the three shared common files are byte-identical to the iteration-1 seal, under which this stage passed. Since then only files outside the homily changed: generation-metadata.tex, research/production-review.md, research/artifacts.json, synthesis.tex and sections/concise/90-apparatus.tex. I read each of those diffs against HEAD for its bearing on the homily. The concise changes alter four References entries (Irenaeus, the Mystagogical Catecheses, Schuster and Nostra aetate) and move the concise title's descriptive line into the subtitle field. The homily quotes, cites and relies on none of these, and its References and note make no claim about the concise study's title or apparatus. The shared generation record changed its revision timestamp to 2026-10-08T18:33:23Z and extended the Droid contribution entry with an account of derive-synthesis iteration 3 that matches the audit and the diff. No homily contribution was added, which is right, because no homily render input changed. The derive-homily iteration-2 audit entry is truthful where I could check it. I rebuilt homily.tex from the current sources in my scratch directory with the pinned Python Markdown. Its auxiliary file and PDF were identical across three passes, and the log has no LaTeX or package warning and no overfull or underfull box. The PDF is 4 letter pages with eleven embedded subset Type 1 fonts, and it is byte-identical to the recorded proof (SHA-256 857e4db160006c23638eb94f8b25c3a2354c7300b38a5f9fee4e70904a9e0af2). Its extracted text differs from the PDF accepted at iteration 1 (2e0675cc...) only in the 'Last revised (UTC)' line. tools/check-generation-metadata passes for the document and for this rebuilt PDF. I recounted the spoken words at 1,465, which matches the note and the audit (about 11.3 minutes at 130 words a minute and 12.2 at 120). The audit's count of checks (component contract plus twelve content-preflight checks) matches the homily-preflight gate. I read the unchanged spoken body through continuously once more. It still makes the one textual argument accepted at iteration 1, from Mt 22:5's neglect for lawful goods through the feast, the roads, Phil 4:12-14 and the garment of charity, to the orations and a practicable response. It needs no new finding. The standing advisory HOM-005 is now cleared by its first required result: the iteration-2 audit records a full silent read-through of the current spoken body, so the note's sentence 'The prose was read through in full ... silently and not aloud' matches the record. Limits: I did not re-verify the unchanged quotations at their source loci, which iterations 0 and 1 checked under identical sealed bytes. No spoken or timed delivery was possible, and none is claimed. Visual acceptance and the refresh of the stale build receipt research/artifacts.json belong to the build-artifacts and visual-review stages. Verdict: PASS."
